From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: dw-mipi-csi2rx: always report progressive frames

set_fmt() copies the caller's v4l2_mbus_framefmt into the sink pad verbatim,
so a caller that leaves the field unset stores V4L2_FIELD_ANY. Link
validation then compares that against a sensor reporting V4L2_FIELD_NONE and
rejects the pipeline:

  v4l2_subdev_link_validate_default: field does not match (source 1, sink 0)
  Link 'ov5648 2-0036':0 -> 'dw-mipi-csi2rx fdfb0000.csi':0 failed validation: -32
  rockchip-cif fdfe0000.video-capture: failed to start pipeline -32

CSI-2 carries progressive frames only, and the driver's own default_format
already says V4L2_FIELD_NONE, so force it rather than trusting the caller.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN g_a/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/dw-mipi-csi2rx.c g_b/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/dw-mipi-csi2rx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/dw-mipi-csi2rx.c	2026-09-18 09:47:53.091395933 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/synopsys/dw-mipi-csi2rx.c	2026-09-18 09:47:53.112045787 +0200
@@ -498,6 +498,14 @@
 	if (!fmt)
 		format->format = default_format;
 
+	/*
+	 * CSI-2 carries progressive frames only. Userspace that leaves the
+	 * field unset would otherwise store V4L2_FIELD_ANY here and every
+	 * link validation against a sensor reporting V4L2_FIELD_NONE would
+	 * fail with -EPIPE.
+	 */
+	format->format.field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
+
 	*sink = format->format;
 
 	/* propagate the format to the source pad */
